    "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
    "name": "MFA and new-fave",
    "readme": "Tutorial showing how to use the Montreal Forced Aligner and new-fave. It uses sample data that can be found on Zenodo. After uploading the data, the next step is to check whether there are any words that are not included in the dictionary (find OOVs). Then you can generate pronunciations of these words using G2P before merging them with the built-in dictionary. Next, the phonetic transcriptions can be aligned to the individual sounds in the audio file. The aligned TextGrid and the original audio file are then input into new-fave to automatically extract the vowel formant measurents.",
    "report": {
        "markdown": "\n# Workflow Execution Report\n\n## Workflow Inputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_inputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow Outputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_outputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow\n```galaxy\nworkflow_display()\n```\n"
    },
